-- ccc6-disorderly.l4 -- ss 173 (Indecent acts), 174 (Nudity), 175 (Causing disturbance, indecent exhibition, loitering), 176 (Obstructing or violence to an officiant; disturbing worship),
-- 177 (Trespassing at night), 180 (Common nuisance) and 182 (Dead body).
-- An offence function answers JUST TRUE when every element is met and NOTHING otherwise (fork F1). Where a section is punishable on summary conviction and states no penalty, s 787(1) is an input (another part).
-- Terms of s 2 and s 150 are seams: the answer of the definition is an input (`s 2 dwelling-house`, `s 2 night`, `s 2 peace officer`, `s 150 public place`, `s 150 sexual organs`).
-- NOT is always written on a line of its own or in brackets.

§ `s 173 Indecent acts`

-- src:3460 | Indecent acts
-- src:3461 | 173 (1) Everyone who wilfully does an indecent act in a public place in the presence of one or more persons, or in any place with intent to insult or offend any person,
-- src:3462 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years; or
-- src:3463 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 173(1) (src:3460-3463)
GIVEN `the person wilfully did an indecent act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 150 public place: the place is a public place` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it was in the presence of one or more persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was done with intent to insult or offend any person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173(1) the conduct is the offence of an indecent act` MEANS
    IF    `the person wilfully did an indecent act`
      AND (   (   `s 150 public place: the place is a public place` EQUALS JUST TRUE
              AND `it was in the presence of one or more persons`)
           OR `it was done with intent to insult or offend any person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone who wilfully does an indecent act in a public place in the presence of one or more persons, or in any place with intent to insult or offend any person"

@ref Criminal Code s 173(1)(a) (src:3462)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 173(1)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 173(1)(b) (src:3463)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 173(1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 173(1) (src:3460-3463)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 173(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:3464 | Exposure
-- src:3465 | (2) Every person who, in any place, for a sexual purpose, exposes their sexual organs to a person who is under the age of 16 years
-- src:3466 | (a) is guilty of an indictable offence and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of 90 days; or
-- src:3467 | (b) is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and is liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of 30 days.
@ref Criminal Code s 173(2) (src:3464-3467)
GIVEN `the person exposed their sexual organs to another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 150 sexual organs: what was exposed` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it was for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age in years of the person to whom they were exposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 173(2) the conduct is the offence of exposure to a person under 16` MEANS
    IF    `the person exposed their sexual organs to another person`
      AND `s 150 sexual organs: what was exposed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `it was for a sexual purpose`
      AND `the age in years of the person to whom they were exposed` LESS THAN 16
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who, in any place, for a sexual purpose, exposes their sexual organs to a person who is under the age of 16 years"

@ref Criminal Code s 173(2)(a) (src:3466)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 173(2)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ninety days`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 173(2)(b) (src:3467)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 173(2)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`, `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, 30, FALSE), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 173(2) (src:3464-3467)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 173(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

§ `s 174 Nudity`

-- src:3473 | Nude
-- src:3474 | (2) For the purposes of this section, a person is nude who is so clad as to offend against public decency or order.
@ref Criminal Code s 174(2) (src:3473-3474)
GIVEN `the person is so clad as to offend against public decency or order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(2) the person is nude` MEANS
    IF `the person is so clad as to offend against public decency or order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person is nude who is so clad as to offend against public decency or order"

-- src:3468 | Nudity
-- src:3469 | 174 (1) Every one who, without lawful excuse,
-- src:3470 | (a) is nude in a public place, or
-- src:3471 | (b) is nude and exposed to public view while on private property, whether or not the property is his own,
-- src:3472 | is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 174(1) (src:3468-3472)
GIVEN `the person acted without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 174(2) the person is nude` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 150 public place: the place is a public place` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is on private property, whether or not the property is the person's own, and is exposed to public view` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(1) the conduct is the offence of nudity` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted without lawful excuse`
      AND `s 174(2) the person is nude` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND (   `s 150 public place: the place is a public place` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR `the person is on private property, whether or not the property is the person's own, and is exposed to public view`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who, without lawful excuse, (a) is nude in a public place, or (b) is nude and exposed to public view while on private property, whether or not the property is his own, is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction"

@ref Criminal Code s 174(1) (src:3472)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 174(1) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 174(1) (src:3468-3472)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 174(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:3475 | Consent of Attorney General
-- src:3476 | (3) No proceedings shall be commenced under this section without the consent of the Attorney General.
@ref Criminal Code s 174(3) (src:3475-3476)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under section 174` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 174(3) no proceedings shall be commenced without the consent of the Attorney General: the bar applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are proceedings under section 174` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No proceedings shall be commenced under this section"
        IF `the Attorney General has consented` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without the consent of the Attorney General"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `s 175 Causing disturbance, indecent exhibition, loitering, etc.`

DECLARE `s 175(1)(a) how the person caused the disturbance` IS ONE OF
    `s 175(1)(a)(i) by fighting`
    `s 175(1)(a)(i) by screaming`
    `s 175(1)(a)(i) by shouting`
    `s 175(1)(a)(i) by swearing`
    `s 175(1)(a)(i) by singing`
    `s 175(1)(a)(i) by using insulting or obscene language`
    `s 175(1)(a)(ii) by being drunk`
    `s 175(1)(a)(iii) by impeding or molesting other persons`
    `s 175(1)(a) in another way`

-- src:3477 | Causing disturbance, indecent exhibition, loitering, etc.
-- src:3478 | 175 (1) Every one who
-- src:3479 | (a) not being in a dwelling-house, causes a disturbance in or near a public place,
-- src:3480 | (i) by fighting, screaming, shouting, swearing, singing or using insulting or obscene language,
-- src:3481 | (ii) by being drunk, or
-- src:3482 | (iii) by impeding or molesting other persons,
-- src:3483 | (b) openly exposes or exhibits an indecent exhibition in a public place,
-- src:3484 | (c) loiters in a public place and in any way obstructs persons who are in that place, or
-- src:3485 | (d) disturbs the peace and quiet of the occupants of a dwelling-house by discharging firearms or by other disorderly conduct in a public place or who, not being an occupant of a dwelling-house comprised in a particular building or structure, disturbs the peace and quiet of the occupants of a dwelling-house comprised in the building or structure by discharging firearms or by other disorderly conduct in any part of a building or structure to which, at the time of such conduct, the occupants of two or more dwelling-houses comprised in the building or structure have access as of right or by invitation, express or implied,
-- src:3486 | is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 175(1) (src:3477-3486)
GIVEN `s 2 dwelling-house: the person is in a dwelling-house` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person causes a disturbance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 150 public place: the disturbance is in or near a public place` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `how the person caused the disturbance` IS A `s 175(1)(a) how the person caused the disturbance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(1)(a) the conduct is the offence of causing a disturbance in or near a public place` MEANS
    IF    `s 2 dwelling-house: the person is in a dwelling-house` EQUALS JUST FALSE
      AND `the person causes a disturbance`
      AND `s 150 public place: the disturbance is in or near a public place` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND NOT (`how the person caused the disturbance` EQUALS `s 175(1)(a) in another way`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every one who (a) not being in a dwelling-house, causes a disturbance in or near a public place, (i) by fighting, screaming, shouting, swearing, singing or using insulting or obscene language, (ii) by being drunk, or (iii) by impeding or molesting other persons"

@ref Criminal Code s 175(1)(b) (src:3483)
GIVEN `the person openly exposes or exhibits an indecent exhibition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 150 public place: the place is a public place` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(1)(b) the conduct is the offence of an indecent exhibition in a public place` MEANS
    IF `the person openly exposes or exhibits an indecent exhibition` AND `s 150 public place: the place is a public place` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) openly exposes or exhibits an indecent exhibition in a public place"

@ref Criminal Code s 175(1)(c) (src:3484)
GIVEN `the person loiters in a public place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 150 public place: the place is a public place` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person in any way obstructs persons who are in that place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(1)(c) the conduct is the offence of loitering in a public place and obstructing persons` MEANS
    IF    `the person loiters in a public place`
      AND `s 150 public place: the place is a public place` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `the person in any way obstructs persons who are in that place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(c) loiters in a public place and in any way obstructs persons who are in that place"

-- (d) has two limbs: a disturbance of the occupants of a dwelling-house by discharging firearms or other disorderly conduct in a public place, or, by a person who is not an occupant of a dwelling-house in a building, in any part of the building to which the occupants of two or more dwelling-houses in it have access.
DECLARE `s 175(1)(d) the conduct` IS ONE OF
    `s 175(1)(d) discharging firearms`
    `s 175(1)(d) other disorderly conduct`
    `s 175(1)(d) neither`

@ref Criminal Code s 175(1)(d) (src:3485)
GIVEN `the person disturbs the peace and quiet of the occupants of a dwelling-house` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct` IS A `s 175(1)(d) the conduct`
      `s 150 public place: the place of the conduct is a public place` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is not an occupant of a dwelling-house comprised in the building or structure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conduct was in a part of the building or structure to which, at the time of the conduct, the occupants of two or more dwelling-houses comprised in it have access as of right or by invitation, express or implied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(1)(d) the conduct is the offence of disturbing the peace and quiet of the occupants of a dwelling-house` MEANS
    IF    `the person disturbs the peace and quiet of the occupants of a dwelling-house`
      AND NOT (`the conduct` EQUALS `s 175(1)(d) neither`)
      AND (   `s 150 public place: the place of the conduct is a public place` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           OR (   `the person is not an occupant of a dwelling-house comprised in the building or structure`
              AND `the conduct was in a part of the building or structure to which, at the time of the conduct, the occupants of two or more dwelling-houses comprised in it have access as of right or by invitation, express or implied`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(d) disturbs the peace and quiet of the occupants of a dwelling-house by discharging firearms or by other disorderly conduct in a public place or who, not being an occupant of a dwelling-house comprised in a particular building or structure, disturbs the peace and quiet of the occupants of a dwelling-house comprised in the building or structure by discharging firearms or by other disorderly conduct in any part of a building or structure to which"

@ref Criminal Code s 175(1) (src:3486)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 175(1) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 175(1) (src:3477-3486)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 175(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- (2) "a summary conviction court may infer from the evidence of a peace officer ... that a disturbance described in paragraph (1)(a) or (d) or an obstruction described in paragraph (1)(c) was caused or occurred": a power of the court, with limits in its own wording: NOTHING outside them.
-- src:3487 | Evidence of peace officer
-- src:3488 | (2) In the absence of other evidence, or by way of corroboration of other evidence, a summary conviction court may infer from the evidence of a peace officer relating to the conduct of a person or persons, whether ascertained or not, that a disturbance described in paragraph (1)(a) or (d) or an obstruction described in paragraph (1)(c) was caused or occurred.
@ref Criminal Code s 175(2) (src:3487-3488)
-- LIMB BY LIMB (sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F9): the no-other-evidence limb is a gate of the where kind, so a failed no-other-evidence limb answers as the guide does (ruling (b) of 2026-11-05): JUST FALSE, listed in the fork register with the other reading (NOTHING). The other limbs are if-gates or scope limits and answer NOTHING (11-12 limit (1); ruling (c) of 2026-11-05).
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the witness is a peace officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the evidence relates to the conduct of a person or persons, whether ascertained or not` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is no other evidence, or the evidence is by way of corroboration of other evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter is a disturbance described in paragraph (1)(a) or (d) or an obstruction described in paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 175(2) a summary conviction court may infer from the evidence of a peace officer that the disturbance or obstruction occurred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `there is no other evidence, or the evidence is by way of corroboration of other evidence`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the absence of other evidence, or by way of corroboration of other evidence"
        IF    `s 2 peace officer: the witness is a peace officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          AND `the evidence relates to the conduct of a person or persons, whether ascertained or not`
          AND `the matter is a disturbance described in paragraph (1)(a) or (d) or an obstruction described in paragraph (1)(c)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the absence of other evidence, or by way of corroboration of other evidence, a summary conviction court may infer from the evidence of a peace officer relating to the conduct of a person or persons, whether ascertained or not, that a disturbance described in paragraph (1)(a) or (d) or an obstruction described in paragraph (1)(c) was caused or occurred"

§ `s 176 Obstructing or violence to or arrest of officiating clergyman`

DECLARE `s 176(1)(a) what the person did` IS ONE OF
    `s 176(1)(a) obstructs`
    `s 176(1)(a) prevents`
    `s 176(1)(a) endeavours to obstruct`
    `s 176(1)(a) endeavours to prevent`
    `s 176(1)(a) none of those`

-- src:3489 | Obstructing or violence to or arrest of officiating clergyman
-- src:3490 | 176 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
-- src:3491 | (a) by threats or force, unlawfully obstructs or prevents or endeavours to obstruct or prevent an officiant from celebrating a religious or spiritual service or performing any other function in connection with their calling, or
-- src:3492 | (b) knowing that an officiant is about to perform, is on their way to perform or is returning from the perform­ance of any of the duties or functions mentioned in paragraph (a)
-- src:3493 | (i) assaults or offers any violence to them, or
-- src:3494 | (ii) arrests them on a civil process, or under the pretence of executing a civil process.
@ref Criminal Code s 176(1) (src:3489-3494)
GIVEN `what the person did to the officiant` IS A `s 176(1)(a) what the person did`
      `it was by threats or force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was to stop the officiant celebrating a religious or spiritual service or performing any other function in connection with their calling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 176(1)(a) the conduct is the offence of obstructing an officiant by threats or force` MEANS
    IF    NOT (`what the person did to the officiant` EQUALS `s 176(1)(a) none of those`)
      AND `it was by threats or force`
      AND `it was unlawful`
      AND `it was to stop the officiant celebrating a religious or spiritual service or performing any other function in connection with their calling`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) by threats or force, unlawfully obstructs or prevents or endeavours to obstruct or prevent an officiant from celebrating a religious or spiritual service or performing any other function in connection with their calling"

DECLARE `s 176(1)(b) what the person did` IS ONE OF
    `s 176(1)(b)(i) assaults or offers violence`
    `s 176(1)(b)(ii) arrests on a civil process, or under the pretence of executing a civil process`
    `s 176(1)(b) neither`

@ref Criminal Code s 176(1)(b) (src:3492-3494)
GIVEN `the person knew that an officiant was about to perform, was on their way to perform or was returning from the performance of any of the duties or functions mentioned in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the person did to the officiant` IS A `s 176(1)(b) what the person did`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 176(1)(b) the conduct is the offence of assaulting or arresting an officiant` MEANS
    IF    `the person knew that an officiant was about to perform, was on their way to perform or was returning from the performance of any of the duties or functions mentioned in paragraph (a)`
      AND NOT (`what the person did to the officiant` EQUALS `s 176(1)(b) neither`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) knowing that an officiant is about to perform, is on their way to perform or is returning from the perform"

@ref Criminal Code s 176(1)(a) to (b) (src:3490)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 176(1) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 176(1) (src:3490)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 176(1) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 176(1) (src:3489-3494)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 176(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

