§ `s 177 Trespassing at night`

-- src:3499 | Trespassing at night
-- src:3500 | 177 Every person who, without lawful excuse, loiters or prowls at night on the property of another person near a dwelling-house situated on that property is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 177 (src:3499-3500)
GIVEN `the person acted without lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person loitered or prowled on the property of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 night: it was at night` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 2 dwelling-house: the place near which the person loitered or prowled is a dwelling-house situated on that property` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 177 the conduct is the offence of trespassing at night` MEANS
    IF    `the person acted without lawful excuse`
      AND `the person loitered or prowled on the property of another person`
      AND `s 2 night: it was at night` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND `s 2 dwelling-house: the place near which the person loitered or prowled is a dwelling-house situated on that property` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who, without lawful excuse, loiters or prowls at night on the property of another person near a dwelling-house situated on that property is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction"

@ref Criminal Code s 177 (src:3500)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 177 the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 177 (src:3499-3500)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 177 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `s 180 Common nuisance`

DECLARE `s 180(2) what the unlawful act or failure endangers or obstructs` IS ONE OF
    `s 180(2)(a) endangers the lives of the public`
    `s 180(2)(a) endangers the safety of the public`
    `s 180(2)(a) endangers the health of the public`
    `s 180(2)(a) endangers the property of the public`
    `s 180(2)(a) endangers the comfort of the public`
    `s 180(2)(b) obstructs the public in the exercise or enjoyment of any right that is common to all the subjects of Her Majesty in Canada`
    `s 180(2) none of those`

-- src:3509 | Definition
-- src:3510 | (2) For the purposes of this section, every one commits a common nuisance who does an unlawful act or fails to discharge a legal duty and thereby
-- src:3511 | (a) endangers the lives, safety, health, property or comfort of the public; or
-- src:3512 | (b) obstructs the public in the exercise or enjoyment of any right that is common to all the subjects of Her Majesty in Canada.
@ref Criminal Code s 180(2) (src:3509-3512)
GIVEN `the person does an unlawful act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to discharge a legal duty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the person thereby does` IS A `s 180(2) what the unlawful act or failure endangers or obstructs`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 180(2) the person commits a common nuisance` MEANS
    IF    (`the person does an unlawful act` OR `the person fails to discharge a legal duty`)
      AND NOT (`what the person thereby does` EQUALS `s 180(2) none of those`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every one commits a common nuisance who does an unlawful act or fails to discharge a legal duty and thereby (a) endangers the lives, safety, health, property or comfort of the public; or (b) obstructs the public in the exercise or enjoyment of any right that is common to all the subjects of Her Majesty in Canada"

-- src:3505 | Common nuisance
-- src:3506 | 180 (1) Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who commits a common nuisance and by doing so
-- src:3507 | (a) endangers the lives, safety or health of the public, or
-- src:3508 | (b) causes physical injury to any person.
@ref Criminal Code s 180(1) (src:3505-3508)
GIVEN `s 180(2) the person commits a common nuisance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `by doing so the person endangers the lives, safety or health of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by doing so the person causes physical injury to any person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 180(1) the conduct is the offence of committing a common nuisance` MEANS
    IF    `s 180(2) the person commits a common nuisance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
      AND (   `by doing so the person endangers the lives, safety or health of the public`
           OR `by doing so the person causes physical injury to any person`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who commits a common nuisance and by doing so (a) endangers the lives, safety or health of the public, or (b) causes physical injury to any person"

@ref Criminal Code s 180(1) (src:3506)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 180(1) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 180(1) (src:3506)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 180(1) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 180(1) (src:3505-3508)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 180 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

§ `s 182 Dead body`

-- src:3514 | Dead body
-- src:3515 | 182 Every person is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years or is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction who
-- src:3516 | (a) neglects, without lawful excuse, to perform any duty that is imposed on him by law or that he undertakes with reference to the burial of a dead human body or human remains, or
-- src:3517 | (b) improperly or indecently interferes with or offers any indignity to a dead human body or human remains, whether buried or not.
@ref Criminal Code s 182 (src:3514-3517)
GIVEN `the person neglected, without lawful excuse, to perform a duty imposed on the person by law or undertaken with reference to the burial of a dead human body or human remains` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person improperly or indecently interfered with, or offered an indignity to, a dead human body or human remains, whether buried or not` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 182 the conduct is the offence concerning a dead human body` MEANS
    IF    `the person neglected, without lawful excuse, to perform a duty imposed on the person by law or undertaken with reference to the burial of a dead human body or human remains`
       OR `the person improperly or indecently interfered with, or offered an indignity to, a dead human body or human remains, whether buried or not`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who (a) neglects, without lawful excuse, to perform any duty that is imposed on him by law or that he undertakes with reference to the burial of a dead human body or human remains, or (b) improperly or indecently interferes with or offers any indignity to a dead human body or human remains, whether buried or not"

@ref Criminal Code s 182 (src:3515)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 182 the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 182 (src:3515)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 182 the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 182 (src:3514-3517)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 182 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
